    "result_text": "Done. The build is green with the full test suite passing.\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`riskFlag` is a derived, read-only boolean on the owner response, true when **any** of the three conditions hold, else false. I followed the codebase's established pattern for computed read-only DTO fields (`locality`, `membershipLevel`, `ownerSegment`, \u2026): a `util` class invoked from a mapstruct `expression` mapping \u2014 no entity field, no pipeline step, no schema/DB change. Because it's derived from already-computed state, it's identical on the create response and on later `GET`s.\n\nThe three conditions map to existing concepts:\n\n- **possible duplicate** \u2192 `owner.getPossibleDuplicate()` (set by `CheckPossibleDuplicate`).\n- **city over soft capacity** \u2192 `owner.getCapacityWarning()` \u2014 the existing soft per-city band (40\u201349, below the hard cap of 50 which rejects the create).\n- **email domain disposable-adjacent** \u2192 a domain that is a sub-domain of a throwaway provider (e.g. `signup.mailinator.com`). Exact disposable domains are already rejected with 400 at validation, so they never reach a persisted owner; the adjacency check flags the near-misses that slip through.\n\nFiles:\n- `util/DisposableEmailDomains.java` (new) \u2014 the single disposable-domain blocklist plus `isBlocked` (exact) and `isDisposableAdjacent` (domain or sub-domain).\n- `util/RiskFlags.java` (new) \u2014 `flagFor(owner)` OR-combining the three conditions.\n- `OwnerEmail.java` \u2014 refactored to reuse `DisposableEmailDomains.isBlocked` instead of its own private copy of the list (removes duplication/drift).\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added the `riskFlag` expression mapping.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `riskFlag` read-only boolean to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` passes (a fully unique owner with no email \u2192 false), and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
